Subject: [PATCH] ubus: keep off the bridge device when built without ubus

bridger's local-tx handling attaches the classifier to the bridge device
itself, at clsact egress. That hook runs before the device's root qdisc, so
a flow leaving the bridge towards a LAN client is redirected straight to the
member port and never passes through the qdisc.

Tomato64 shapes download traffic exactly there: the Bandwidth Limiter and
the quota "limit speed" feature both put an HTB tree on br0..brN. Measured
on a GL-BE14000 with a 10 Mbit tbf on br0: with local-tx active the shaper
saw 0 packets and the traffic went out unshaped; with this change it counted
every packet and held the rate at 10 Mbit.

Upstream exposes this as the bridge_local_tx option, default on, but it can
only be changed over ubus, and Tomato64 builds bridger without ubus (ubusd
only runs while WiFi is up). So make the no-ubus build behave as
bridge_local_tx=0: report the bridge device as blacklisted, which keeps the
classifier off it. Bridge member ports are unaffected, so flows between LAN
devices (including LAN <-> WiFi and the hardware path) work as before.
---
diff --git a/ubus.h b/ubus.h
index 8c28b24..6a7d6cd 100644
--- a/ubus.h
+++ b/ubus.h
@@ -20,7 +20,8 @@ static inline void bridger_ubus_stop(void)
 }
 static inline bool bridger_ubus_dev_blacklisted(struct device *dev)
 {
-	return false;
+	/* bridge_local_tx = 0: leave the bridge device itself alone */
+	return dev->br != NULL;
 }
 static inline bool bridger_ubus_dev_name_blacklisted(struct device *dev)
 {
